/T (Being Over-Specific: While writing a directive, delegates need to be over-specific about the content of their directive. Appointed subjects can go to the wrong region, can kill the wrong person, can do the wrong thing if the region, person or action is not mentioned with adequate details in the directive, which is a non-specific directive. Additionally, a directive must be able to answer WH questions \(Turkish: 5N1K\) \(who, what, where, when, why, which, whose, how, how many, etc. \). Furthermore, explanation of sources is exceedingly pivotal as delegates have better mention about the fulfillment of required sources such as money, fuel, water, and food. )
