/E (Nomaskible is immediately recognizable because of one very simple detail: he doesn't wear a mask.But his story goes considerably deeper than his appearance. In his own universe, Nomaskible had a close relationship with William Clockwell. Some says that was a sexual relation. Unlike most of the other variants, he clearly retained strong emotional attachments to someone from his original life. That becomes important during the Invincible War. After destroying parts of the mainstream universe, the surviving variants gather at the Grayson house. When Maskvincible explains that he joined the war because he wanted Angstrom to find him another version of Debbie, Nomaskible quietly admits that he misses his own William.That small moment gives him a surprisingly different character from the rest of the group. He's still responsible for the destruction caused during the war, but it's clear that his original life still means something to him. )
/Pg 37 0 R
/K [1]
>>
